#: src/config.md:1
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:3
msgid "Configuration format"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:5
msgid ""
"You can configure maturin in `tool.maturin` section of [`pyproject.toml`]"
"(https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/pyproject-toml/"
"#arbitrary-tool-configuration-the-tool-table)."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:7
msgid "Configuration keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:9
msgid "Cargo options"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:11
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[tool.maturin]\n"
"# Build artifacts with the specified Cargo profile\n"
"profile = \"release\"\n"
"# For \"editable\" builds, use the specified Cargo profile,\n"
"# e.g. to use \"dev\" builds for local development\n"
"# (uses `profile` if this key is not set)\n"
"editable-profile = \"release\"\n"
"# List of features to activate\n"
"features = [\"foo\", \"bar\"]\n"
"# Features can also be conditional on the target Python version\n"
"# using PEP 440 version specifiers:\n"
"# features = [\n"
"#   \"always-on-feature\",\n"
"#   { feature = \"pyo3/abi3-py311\", python-version = \">=3.11\" },\n"
"#   { feature = \"pyo3/abi3-py38\", python-version = \"<3.11\" },\n"
"# ]\n"
"# Activate all available features\n"
"all-features = false\n"
"# Do not activate the `default` feature\n"
"no-default-features = false\n"
"# Cargo manifest path\n"
"manifest-path = \"Cargo.toml\"\n"
"# Require Cargo.lock and cache are up to date\n"
"frozen = false\n"
"# Require Cargo.lock is up to date\n"
"locked = false\n"
"# Override a configuration value (unstable)\n"
"config = []\n"
"# Unstable (nightly-only) flags to Cargo, see 'cargo -Z help' for details\n"
"unstable-flags = []\n"
"# Extra arguments that will be passed to rustc as `cargo rustc [...] -- "
"[...] [arg1] [arg2]`\n"
"rustc-args = []\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:46
msgid ""
"These are `cargo` build options, refer Cargo documentation [here](https://"
"doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-rustc.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:48
msgid "maturin options"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:50
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[tool.maturin]\n"
"# Python import name of the built extension module.\n"
"# Accepts dotted names like \"my_package._native\" so the Rust extension is\n"
"# installed as a submodule (useful for mixed Python/Rust projects).\n"
"# See the project layout docs for a full example.\n"
"module-name = \"my_package._native\"\n"
"# Include additional files\n"
"include = []\n"
"# Exclude files\n"
"exclude = []\n"
"# Bindings type\n"
"bindings = \"pyo3\"\n"
"# Control the platform tag and PyPI compatibility\n"
"compatibility = \"pypi\"\n"
"# auditwheel mode, possible values are repair, check and skip\n"
"auditwheel = \"repair\"\n"
"# Don't check for manylinux compliance, deprecated in favor of auditwheel = "
"\"skip\"\n"
"skip-auditwheel = false\n"
"# Python source directory\n"
"python-source = \"src\"\n"
"# Python packages to include\n"
"python-packages = [\"foo\", \"bar\"]\n"
"# Path to the wheel data directory (see the Data section of the project "
"layout\n"
"# docs). Defaults to looking for `<module-name>.data` next to the project "
"root\n"
"# when that directory exists. Relative paths are resolved from the project "
"root.\n"
"data = \"my_package.data\"\n"
"# Strip the library for minimum file size\n"
"strip = true\n"
"# Source distribution generator,\n"
"# supports cargo (default) and git.\n"
"sdist-generator = \"cargo\"\n"
"# Include the Windows import library (.dll.lib or .dll.a) in the wheel.\n"
"# This is useful when distributing shared libraries that other programs\n"
"# need to link against at compile time.\n"
"include-import-lib = false\n"
"# Use base Python executable instead of venv Python executable in PEP 517 "
"build.\n"
"#\n"
"# This can help avoid unnecessary rebuilds, as the Python executable does "
"not change\n"
"# every time. It should not be set when the sdist build requires packages "
"installed\n"
"# in venv. This can also be set with the `MATURIN_PEP517_USE_BASE_PYTHON` "
"environment\n"
"# variable.\n"
"use-base-python = false\n"
"# Shell command run during Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO) profile "
"generation.\n"
"# Required when building with `--pgo` / `MATURIN_PGO`. Executed in a "
"temporary\n"
"# virtualenv with the instrumented wheel installed.\n"
"# Example: \"python -m pytest tests/benchmarks\"\n"
"pgo-command = \"python -m pytest tests/benchmarks\"\n"
"# Select which Cargo compile targets to build when the crate defines more "
"than\n"
"# one matching target. Each entry is an object with a required `name` (as "
"in\n"
"# Cargo.toml) and an optional `kind` (`bin`, `cdylib`, `dylib`, `lib`, "
"`rlib`,\n"
"# or `staticlib`). This is unrelated to `[tool.maturin.target.<triple>]` "
"below.\n"
"# targets = [\n"
"#   { name = \"my_extension\", kind = \"cdylib\" },\n"
"# ]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:107
msgid "`module-name`"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:109
msgid ""
"By default maturin derives the extension module name from the Cargo package "
"name. Set `module-name` to override that, including with a dotted import "
"path such as `my_package._native`. That places the compiled extension inside "
"a Python package, which is the usual layout for mixed Python/Rust projects."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:114
msgid ""
"See [Import Rust as a submodule of your project](./project_layout.md#import-"
"rust-as-a-submodule-of-your-project) for a complete example (including "
"matching `#[pymodule]` / `#[pyo3(name = ...)]` changes)."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:118
msgid "`data`"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:120
msgid ""
"Path to a wheel [data directory](https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/"
"specifications/binary-distribution-format/#the-data-directory) whose "
"contents are installed into the corresponding wheel install schemes (`data`, "
"`scripts`, `headers`, `purelib`, `platlib`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:124
msgid ""
"If unset, maturin uses `<module-name>.data` at the project root when that "
"directory exists. Relative paths are resolved from the project root."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:127
msgid ""
"See [Data](./project_layout.md#data) for the expected subdirectory layout."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:129
msgid "`targets`"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:131
msgid ""
"`targets` filters which Cargo compile targets maturin builds when a crate "
"exposes several candidates (for example multiple `cdylib` or `bin` targets). "
"It is **not** the same as `[tool.maturin.target.<triple>]`, which configures "
"per-architecture options such as the macOS deployment target."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:136
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[tool.maturin]\n"
"# Only build these Cargo targets (name must match Cargo.toml)\n"
"targets = [\n"
"  { name = \"my_extension\", kind = \"cdylib\" },\n"
"  { name = \"my_cli\", kind = \"bin\" },\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:145
msgid ""
"`name` is required. `kind` is optional; when set it must match one of `bin`, "
"`cdylib`, `dylib`, `lib`, `rlib`, or `staticlib`."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:148
msgid "`pgo-command`"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:150
msgid ""
"Command used for the profile-training step of Profile-Guided Optimization. "
"Required when you pass `--pgo` (or set `MATURIN_PGO`). Maturin runs the "
"command in a temporary virtualenv after installing the instrumented wheel."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:154
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[tool.maturin]\n"
"pgo-command = \"python -m pytest tests/benchmarks\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:159
msgid ""
"See the `--pgo` option under [Build](./distribution.md) for the overall "
"three-phase flow."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:162
msgid "`generate-ci`"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:164
msgid ""
"Defaults for `maturin generate-ci` (currently GitHub Actions). CLI flags "
"that overlap with this table are deprecated in favor of pyproject "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:167
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[tool.maturin.generate-ci.github]\n"
"# Enable a pytest job in the generated workflow\n"
"pytest = true\n"
"# Use zig for manylinux cross compilation\n"
"zig = true\n"
"# Skip artifact attestation steps\n"
"skip-attestation = false\n"
"# Publish with PyPI trusted publishing (OIDC) instead of an API token\n"
"trusted-publishing = true\n"
"# Optional GitHub Actions environment name for the release job\n"
"publishing-environment = \"release\"\n"
"# Extra arguments passed to maturin on every platform\n"
"args = \"--find-interpreter\"\n"
"\n"
"# Per-platform overrides. Each platform may set a simple `targets` list\n"
"# (architecture names such as \"x86_64\" / \"aarch64\") or a detailed\n"
"# `[[tool.maturin.generate-ci.github.<platform>.target]]` array, plus "
"shared\n"
"# keys: runner, manylinux, container, docker-options, rust-toolchain,\n"
"# rustup-components, before-script-linux, args.\n"
"[tool.maturin.generate-ci.github.linux]\n"
"runner = \"ubuntu-22.04\"\n"
"manylinux = \"2_28\"\n"
"targets = [\"x86_64\", \"aarch64\"]\n"
"\n"
"[tool.maturin.generate-ci.github.macos]\n"
"targets = [\"aarch64\"]\n"
"\n"
"# Detailed per-target form (mutually exclusive with `targets` on the same "
"platform):\n"
"# [[tool.maturin.generate-ci.github.linux.target]]\n"
"# arch = \"x86_64\"\n"
"# manylinux = \"2_28\"\n"
"#\n"
"# [[tool.maturin.generate-ci.github.linux.target]]\n"
"# arch = \"aarch64\"\n"
"# runner = \"self-hosted-arm64\"\n"
"# before-script-linux = \"yum install -y openssl-devel\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:206
msgid ""
"Supported platform tables under `[tool.maturin.generate-ci.github]` are "
"`linux`, `musllinux`, `windows`, `macos`, `emscripten`, and `android`."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:209
msgid ""
"See [GitHub Actions](./distribution.md#github-actions) for usage of `maturin "
"generate-ci` and trusted publishing details."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:212
msgid ""
"The `[tool.maturin.include]` and `[tool.maturin.exclude]` configuration are "
"inspired by [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/docs/pyproject/#exclude-and-"
"include)."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:216
msgid ""
"Glob patterns are resolved relative to the directory containing `pyproject."
"toml`. When using `python-source` (e.g. `python-source = \"src/python\"`), "
"patterns are also tried relative to the `python-source` directory if they "
"don't match relative to `pyproject.toml`. This means you can use a single "
"pattern like `include = [\"mypackage/data.txt\"]` and it will work for both "
"sdist and wheel targets: the sdist will include the file at its original "
"location (`src/python/mypackage/data.txt`), and the wheel will include it at "
"the package-relative path (`mypackage/data.txt`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:225
msgid "To specify files or globs directly:"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:227
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"include = [\"path/**/*\", \"some/other/file\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:231
msgid "To specify a specific target format (`sdist` or `wheel`):"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:233
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"include = [\n"
"  { path = \"path/**/*\", format = \"sdist\" },\n"
"  { path = \"all\", format = [\"sdist\", \"wheel\"] },\n"
"  { path = \"for/wheel/**/*\", format = \"wheel\" }\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:241
msgid ""
"The default behavior applies these configurations to both `sdist` and "
"`wheel` targets."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:244
msgid ""
"To include files generated by a Cargo build script (`build.rs`) from the "
"crate's `OUT_DIR`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:247
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"include = [\n"
"  { path = \"cpu_features.json\", from = \"out-dir\", to = \"my_package/"
"\" },\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:253
msgid ""
"The `path` is a glob pattern relative to `OUT_DIR`, and `to` specifies the "
"target directory inside the wheel. This only applies to wheel builds (not "
"sdist), since `OUT_DIR` does not exist until `cargo build` runs."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:257
msgid ""
"To include files from a different workspace member's `OUT_DIR`, specify the "
"crate name:"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:260
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"include = [\n"
"  { path = \"generated/*.py\", from = \"out-dir\", to = \"my_package/\", "
"crate-name = \"my-other-crate\" },\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:266
msgid "SBOM options"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:268
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[tool.maturin.sbom]\n"
"# Generate a CycloneDX SBOM for the Rust dependency tree.\n"
"# Defaults to true when the sbom feature is enabled.\n"
"rust = true\n"
"# Generate a CycloneDX SBOM for external shared libraries grafted during\n"
"# auditwheel repair. Defaults to true when repair copies libraries.\n"
"auditwheel = true\n"
"# Additional SBOM files to include in the wheel.\n"
"# Paths are relative to the project root.\n"
"include = [\"sboms/vendor.cdx.json\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:281
msgid "See the [SBOM](./sbom.md) page for more details."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:283
msgid "target specific maturin options"
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:285
msgid ""
"Currently only macOS deployment target SDK version can be configured for "
"`x86_64-apple-darwin` and `aarch64-apple-darwin` targets, other targets have "
"no options yet."
msgstr ""

#: src/config.md:289
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[tool.maturin.target.<triple>]\n"
"# macOS deployment target SDK version\n"
"macos-deployment-target = \"11.0\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
